Vendored from the Ibex affine-arithmetic plugin.

    repository  https://github.com/ibex-team/ibex-affine
    commit      e11099be57bf960747571366adf215e59b0b79bd
    date        2021-06-14

Why vendored rather than built as an external plugin: the plugin's own
CMakeLists expects an *installed* Ibex and produces a separate libibex-affine.
We need affine arithmetic inside libibex itself, because ibexopt-ml selects the
linear relaxation at run time and has to carry both. The sources are used
verbatim -- they compile unchanged against this tree -- and only the build
glue (src/affine/CMakeLists.txt) is ours.

To re-sync with upstream:

    python3 src/affine/resync.py            # reports the diff against upstream
    python3 src/affine/resync.py --apply    # overwrites the vendored sources

